+
+# Community moderation hides comments after three reports
+
+## Context
+
+Readers asked for a way to respond under posts. Product would not ship
+comments that one bad actor can fill with spam, and there is no moderator on
+call, so the community itself has to keep the space clean.
+
+## Decision
+
+- Any signed-in user may comment on any post (1 to 2000 characters). A guest
+  is redirected to `/login`, like a guest trying to write a post.
+- A comment is deleted for real (no soft delete) by its author or by the
+  author of the post it sits on; everyone else gets 403. Deleting a post
+  removes its comments and their reports.
+- Any signed-in user may report a comment. Reports live in `comment_reports`
+  with a unique `(comment_id, user_id)` pair, so a repeated report by the
+  same user is a no-op and the row count is the distinct-reporter count.
+- Once `HIDE_COMMENT_REPORT_THRESHOLD` (3) distinct users have reported a
+  comment, the post page omits it for every viewer, the comment's author and
+  the post's author included. The row stays in `comments` for later review;
+  a review screen is out of scope.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Spam disappears without staff involvement once three readers flag it, at the
+cost of three colluding accounts being able to hide a legitimate comment.
+Hidden comments are never lost, so a future review screen can restore or
+purge them. The threshold is a single constant in `app/Models/Comment.ts`.
